{
 "manufacturer": "ABB",
 "manufacturer_slug": "abb",
 "model": "CMS-700 circuit monitoring system control unit (Modbus RTU / TCP)",
 "model_slug": "cms-700",
 "short_model": "CMS-700",
 "aliases": [
  "CMS-700",
  "CMS700",
  "ABB CMS-700",
  "CMS-700 control unit"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "Power meter (branch circuit monitoring)",
 "applies_to": "ABB CMS-700 control unit with up to 96 CMS branch current sensors, per the CMS-700 user manual (Modbus and SNMP mapping chapter).",
 "summary": "The CMS-700 control unit measures mains voltage, current, power and energy and collects up to 96 open-core or solid-core branch current sensors. It serves everything over Modbus RTU (RS-485) and Modbus TCP on port 8001. Branch currents are 16-bit values in 0.01 A; mains values and branch power/energy are 32-bit, high word first.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": 19200,
  "parity": "Even",
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": 1,
  "tcp_port": 8001
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "The mapping table prints each address in hex (with the decimal beside it), and sensor 1 sits at 0000h, so the printed value is the request address with no offset. The manual has no example frame."
 },
 "default_word_order": "ABCD",
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "CMS-700 User manual - Circuit Monitoring System",
  "doc_number": "2CCC481011M0201 Rev. C",
  "revision_date": "2018-09",
  "url": "https://library.e.abb.com/public/ae914775dba84d5ea4ed896c6c0378f9/CMS%20Manual_web.pdf",
  "pages": "Modbus encoding p. 54; RS-485 settings p. 55; data formats and special values pp. 56-57; mapping table pp. 63-67"
 },
 "notes": [
  "The manual says multi-register data has the most significant part in the lowest address (high word first).",
  "Per-sensor blocks repeat for sensors 1-96: TRMS 0000h-005Fh, AC 0100h-015Fh, DC 0200h-025Fh, min 0400h+, max 0800h+, hold 0C00h+, polarity 2000h+, power factor 7300h+ (one register each); branch power 2200h+ and energy 2300h+ (two registers each). Only the first entries are listed.",
  "Special values: 7FF0h = data pending, 7FFCh = sensor not reachable, 7FFDh = data type disabled, 7FFEh = overload, 7FFFh = no such sensor (FFFF7FFxh for 32-bit values).",
  "The table has a few misprints in its summary rows (the last AC sensor row shows 005F for 351; the group 2 energy row repeats 9'472); this map lists only rows whose hex and decimal agree.",
  "The frame description lists 1 stop bit; parity can be even (default), odd or none. Data bits are not stated.",
  "Left out: sensor serial/version blocks (1000h+), branch and group names, phase/group assignment registers and the threshold alarm block (8100h+).",
  "Group energy (2500h+, 100 Wh steps) is left out because the table prints the same decimal address (9'472) for groups 1 and 2."
 ],
